* ============================================================================
* CD74HC4066 - one channel of the quad bilateral switch, behavioural model (2026-09-28)
* Not a TI model.  Values from TI's CD74HC4066 data sheet (HTML version, read 2026-09-28):
*   on-resistance at VCC 4.5 V ........ about 35 ohm typ     -> RON
*   control input ...................... HC CMOS levels; modelled as a smooth threshold at VDD/2
*   switch turn-on / turn-off delay .... max 20 / 30 ns at 4.5 V, about 10 ns typ at 5 V  -> TON (one RC for both)
*   off-state leakage .................. max 0.1 uA (not modelled; the switch is an ideal 10 GOhm when off)
* Pins: A B CTRL VDD VSS.  CTRL high = switch closed.
* NOT MODELLED: Ron change with signal voltage, charge injection, channel capacitances, leakage.
* ============================================================================
.SUBCKT CD74HC4066 A B CTRL VDD VSS PARAMS: RON=35 ROFF=10G TON=10n
BC c1 VSS V=0.5+0.5*tanh((V(CTRL,VSS)-0.5*V(VDD,VSS))/0.05)
RD c1 c2 1k
CD c2 VSS {TON/0.69/1k}
BS A B I=V(A,B)*(min(max(V(c2,VSS),0),1)/RON+1/ROFF)
RIN CTRL VSS 1G
.ENDS CD74HC4066
